    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1423">

                <pb facs="0937" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg821"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.42/325.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi><anchor n="124"
                        xml:id="d1423-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s June 8. Spanish Vice Consul in the name of Spanish colony yesterday
                    requested me to request State Department to take no further action on the
                    question of enforced loans and stated that payments which have been made were
                    voluntary and that Spaniards have made no complaint. Governor General Caballero
                    has distributed circulars calling a meeting of Spanish colony at Governor’s
                    palace for next Sunday morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1423-f1" n="124" type="source" xml:id="d1423-f1-content">
                <p>Communicated to the Spanish Ambassador June 19, 1914.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
